hey guys it's Jonah here if having bad  knees is your excuse for not exercising  what the truth is that should not stop  you from doing lower body movements I'm  gonna share with you the do's and don'ts  when it comes to working out with bad  knees and how these exercises can help  to prevent and reduce injuries now  before we get started if you haven't yet  subscribed to my YouTube channel be sure  to do so ok and turn on your  notification button so that you will get  notified every time I share a new  workout video recipe or fitness tip  avoid deep squats deep squats are great  to work on your legs and glutes if done  properly however if you suffer from bad  knees  this can cause further pain because it  involves an extreme bending motion and  it can put high amounts of stress on  your knee joints if you don't perform  deep squats properly over time incorrect  form can also cause a knee and back  injuries  hence it is extremely important to check  your posture when exercising perform  partial squats instead start in a  neutral position with both legs  shoulder-width apart and toes pointed  forward only squat as low as 45 degrees  without going too deep this partial  movement will not cause excessive stress  on your knees eventually as you recover  or experience less pain on your knees  then you can slowly squat  deeper avoid lunges if done properly  lunges are a great functional workout as  it strengthens your legs hips and core  muscles although this might seem like a  really simple move lunges can be  difficult to perform especially if your  knees are weak or if you are recovering  from knee injuries this movement  requires a good amount of stabilization  on your legs and core hence it can place  lots of stress on your knees if they are  weak start by performing bridging  instead bridging targets and strengthens  the glutes hamstrings hips core and  lower back muscles without stressing out  the knees lie on your back with your  knees bent and arms by your sides push  your heels into the floor squeeze the  butt and lift your hips off the floor  until your shoulders hips  and these are in a straight line hold  for about two to three counts then  slowly lower the hips and repeat because  you're performing the movement while  lying down this will not place much  stress on your knee joints but at the  same time you're strengthening your  lower body muscles avoid kicking bent  knees are highly strained when you snap  your leg to kick when you kick with high  impact and at a fast pace that sudden  jerk can be really tough on your joints  and this can put greater stress on your  knees if you keep on kicking with a Rome  technique over time you can overuse the  muscles around your knees causing  chronic knee injury perform side leg  raises this exercise can help strengthen  your thigh muscles and shape your legs  stand shoulder width apart with toes  pointed forward as you brace your core  extend and lift one leg out to the side  in a fully controlled manner squeeze the  glutes and thighs right at the top and  repeat on the opposite leg avoid fast or  jerky movements remember to always  engage your core avoid jumping high  impact exercises such as jumping can  only worsen your knee pain high impact  movements shock your knee joints and  place lots of stress on the knees when  you land  jumping places a force of two to three  times your body weight across your knees  which can increase the potential for  injury if you have knee problems you  should avoid jumps that require a very  deep knee bend or could torque than knee  on landing perform step ups low impact  activities such as step ups is more  suitable and can be just as effective  you can use a stepper staircase box or  even a chair to do step ups this  movement will not create as much stress  on your knees but you're still able to  get a good sweaty cardio workout from it  avoid high knee jumps again exercises  that involve jumping like high knee  jumps which focus on increasing muscle  power can be tough on the knee joints  especially when landing the high impact  movement of this exercise and repeating  it at a very fast pace may cause you to  compromise on proper form which can put  your knees at  higher risk of injuries that gentle and  perform knee lifts instead this exercise  works on your entire lower body while  challenging your balance at the same  time so stand tall with your feet  shoulder-width apart brace your core and  slowly raise one knee upward to meet  your hands at a 90 degree angle lower  and change sides as you raise your leg  be sure to engage your core to keep your  balance and feel the contraction on your  lower abs a void treadmill running  weather outdoors or on a treadmill is  also a high-impact exercise that creates  a great deal of stress on your knees  running can stress the knee with up to 8  times the force of walking so if you  have a pre-existing knee damage or if  you're extremely overweight running may  not be the best option for you perform  elliptical instead the elliptical  machine mimics the motion of running -  at the high impact making it a far  better and safer choice when you have  knee pain this is a low impact cardio  workout that uses both the legs and arms  for power the circular movement helps  provide an excellent new range of motion  hip flexion and extension and because  you're fully supported by the machine it  does not strain your ankle and knee  joints and can be safely performed even  with an inflamed knee so stop doing  exercises that can hurt and worsen your  weak or inflamed knees and start  performing the right and safe exercises  that can actually help you to strengthen  your legs and knees to prevent any  future injuries or stiffness and to  perform each exercise for 15 to 20  repetitions and a total of 2 to 3 sets  be sure to like this video share down  with someone who might be having bad  knees and do also check out more workout  videos and fitness tips on my channel  don't forget to hit the subscribe button  and get notified when I upload new  videos every week all the best
 

